4.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: The hinge question is settled to E. Chicago Symphony Orchestra's Education Center as the non-example.

Core hinge definition retained from *Places of Learning: Media, Architecture, Pedagogy*: a material or performative threshold that literally stages inside in relation to outside — public/private, institutional/domestic, self/other — and reconfigures personal/social boundaries.

Sustained hinge illustrations Ellsworth returns to, now unanimously endorsed across rounds:
* U.S. Holocaust Memorial Museum – entrance plaza/ramp/Hall of Witness/Hall of Remembrance sequence as memorial-civic threshold;
* Jane Addams Hull-House Museum – settlement-house porch/entry and domestic/public rooms as porous neighbourhood/institution threshold;
* Manhattan Children’s Museum’s Art Inside Out / Art Outside – children’s work moved from interior onto exterior fence/street and back;
* Anna Deavere Smith’s verbatim documentary theatre – *Fires in the Mirror* / *Twilight: Los Angeles, 1992* as performative hinge of testimony/performer/audience;
* Bravehearts: Men in Skirts – embodied/community performative hinge on gendered inside/outside, private embodiment/public display, discussed in performative pedagogy section alongside Smith.

Round 0 split on Bravehearts vs E. Colleagues 10,12,2,3,4 initially argued Bravehearts is developed as embodied/community performance hinge; colleagues 11,6,8 argued it is not a *Places of Learning* case. Round 2 flipped: colleagues 11,6,8 explicitly now include Bravehearts as a hinge case alongside Smith, and all 14 colleagues endorsed E as outlier. Round 3 consensus complete.

Round 4 public responses: all 14 colleagues select E. Chicago Symphony Orchestra's Education Center. No dissent. Consistent rationale: E is described as programmatic outreach/education with conventionally bounded learning spaces, lacking a material architectural or performative inside/outside threshold operation. It is not developed as a hinge case in the volume.

Current belief: A, B, C, D, F are all used as pedagogical hinge illustrations; E is the only option not used. Disagreement about Bravehearts is resolved toward inclusion. No remaining credible alternative.

